# Frontend API Usage

- Base URL: `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` with fallback `http://localhost:3000`
- See `apps/intersfrontend/.env.example` for local env setup
- Use `fetch` unless the team introduces a shared API helper later
- Always handle network failures (`.catch` or try/catch) and show a user-readable message
- Parse JSON only after a successful response when needed; check `res.ok` for non-2xx
- Do not hardcode production URLs in components
- Keep API calls out of deeply nested UI when possible — fetch in the parent or a small helper

## Example pattern

```javascript
const API_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3000';

fetch(`${API_URL}/health`)
  .then((res) => {
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
    return res.json();
  })
  .then((data) => { /* update state */ })
  .catch(() => { /* set error message in UI */ });
```
